<title>USA: U.S. May housing starts fell 4.8 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. May housing starts fell 4.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE: May     Apr (Prev)     Mar (Prev)   May97/96</p>
<p> -Starts    -4.8    -0.7    2.6    -4.8   -7.7	 -5.4</p>
<p> -Permits    0.1    -1.0   -0.8     1.3    1.3	 -0.1</p>
<p> RATES	 May     Apr (Prev)     Mar (Prev)   May 1996</p>
<p> -Starts   1,397   1,468  1,473   1,479  1,435	1,476</p>
<p> -Permits  1,443   1,442  1,446   1,457  1,457	1,457</p>
<p> STARTS:     May     Apr (Prev)     Mar (Prev)   May 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,088   1,116  1,118   1,142  1,115	1,142</p>
<p> -Multiple   309     352    355     337    320	  334</p>
<p> PERMITS     May     Apr (Prev)     Mar (Prev)   May 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,056   1,060  1,064   1,034  1,034	1,101</p>
<p> -Multiple   387     382    382     423    423	  356</p>
<p>   MAY STARTS--Pct--Rate     MAY PERMITS-Pct---Rate</p>
<p> -NorthEast   -8.1   124    -Northeast   4.7   133</p>
<p> -Midwest     UNCH   293    -Midwest    -6.6   295</p>
<p> -South	-11.3   615    -South	-2.6   634</p>
<p> -West	   5.2   365    -West	  9.5   381</p>
<p>May starts of single-family homes were down 2.5 percent from April, and multiple-unit starts fell 12.2 percent. May permits for single-family units fell 0.4 percent, while permits for multiple-unit dwellings rose 1.3 percent.</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  May   Apr   Mar  May96</p>
<p>  Starts     136   140   120   144</p>
<p>  Permits    133   137   120   141</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast May starts at a 1.47 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>The department said housing starts in May marked the third straight monthly decline for the first time since January through March 1995.</p>
